<procedure name="process-pages">
  <description>
    Process saved pages from browser captures. Classifies content,
    converts to appropriate card types, and asks questions when unsure.
  </description>

  <step id="intake">
    <description>Classify and route saved pages</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell>
        saved=$(ls box/inbox/pages-saved/*.record.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        todo=$(ls box/inbox/pages-todo/*.record.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        count=$((saved + todo))
        if [ "$count" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $count page(s) to process ($saved saved, $todo todo)"
      </shell>
      <why>No saved pages to process</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="sonnet" max-turns="30">
        You are processing saved web pages in a Callback Box.

        YOUR TASK:
        Review pages in box/inbox/pages-saved/ and box/inbox/pages-todo/ and route them
        to appropriate destinations. Each page is a record.card containing markdown
        extracted from the web page, plus metadata (URL, site name, excerpt).

        STEP 0 - READ THE INTAKE GUIDE:
        Check if config/intake-guide.md exists. If it does, read it to understand:
        - How the user wants different content types handled
        - Which card types to convert to (recipe, record, etc.)
        - Where things should be routed
        - What to ask about vs. decide autonomously

        If no guide exists, create one with a minimal starting point:
        ```
        # Intake Guide

        Guidelines for processing saved pages. This file is updated over time
        as preferences become clearer.

        ## Content Types

        - **Recipes**: Convert to recipe.card in store/recipes/
        - **Articles to read later**: Keep as record.card, move to box/pool/reading/
        - **Reference material**: Keep as record.card, move to store/catalogs/Reference/
        - **Other**: Ask a question about what to do

        ## Preferences

        (None yet — will be updated based on feedback)
        ```

        STEP 1 - READ ALL PAGES:
        Read each record.card in both directories. Examine:
        - The &lt;name&gt; (page title)
        - The &lt;description&gt; (excerpt)
        - The &lt;content&gt; (full markdown of the page)
        - The &lt;sources&gt; (URL and site info)
        - Which directory it's in (pages-saved = archival, pages-todo = action needed)

        STEP 2 - CLASSIFY AND ROUTE:
        For each page, decide what to do based on the intake guide and content:

        **If it's clearly a recipe:**
        Create a proper recipe.card in store/recipes/:
        ```
        cb create store/recipes/Recipe_Name.recipe.card
        ```
        Then edit it to extract structured recipe data (title, yield, ingredients, steps)
        from the markdown content. Use the recipe schema format.

        **If it's clearly reference material (pages-saved):**
        Move to an appropriate catalog:
        ```
        cb mv box/inbox/pages-saved/Page.record.card store/catalogs/Category/
        ```

        **If it's a pages-todo item with clear action:**
        Route based on what the action should be:
        - Reading material → box/pool/reading/
        - Reference material → store/catalogs/&lt;category&gt;/

        **If you're unsure what to do:**
        Create a question card asking the user. This is ENCOURAGED — don't guess:
        ```
        cb create box/questions/intake-Page_Name.question.card
        ```
        Then edit it:
        ```xml
        &lt;question status="pending" answered-by="process-pages"&gt;
          &lt;memo&gt;
            Saved page: "Page Title" from example.com
            Content appears to be: [your assessment]
            [Brief summary of what the page contains]
          &lt;/memo&gt;
          &lt;context ref="box/inbox/pages-saved/Page.record.card" /&gt;
          &lt;prompt&gt;What would you like to do with this page?&lt;/prompt&gt;
          &lt;input type="select"&gt;
            &lt;option id="recipe"&gt;Convert to recipe&lt;/option&gt;
            &lt;option id="reference"&gt;Save as reference&lt;/option&gt;
            &lt;option id="read-later"&gt;Add to reading list&lt;/option&gt;
            &lt;option id="trash"&gt;Trash it&lt;/option&gt;
          &lt;/input&gt;
        &lt;/question&gt;
        ```

        Adjust the options based on what makes sense for the content.
        Include enough context in &lt;memo&gt; that the user can decide without
        re-reading the whole page.

        GUIDELINES:
        - **Ask questions liberally.** It's better to ask than to misroute.
          Over time the intake guide will capture preferences and you'll ask less.
        - For pages-saved items: the user wanted to keep this. Don't trash unless
          it's clearly an error (blank page, login wall, etc.)
        - For pages-todo items: the user wanted something DONE with this. Think about
          what action makes sense.
        - When converting to recipe cards, extract the full structured data —
          don't just copy the markdown into a record.
        - After successfully routing a page, the original record.card in inbox
          should be removed (moved to its destination or trashed).

        OUTPUT: For each page, state your decision:
          RECIPE: [filename] → store/recipes/[name].recipe.card
          REFERENCE: [filename] → store/catalogs/[category]/
          READING: [filename] → box/pool/reading/
          QUESTION: [filename] → asking user
          TRASH: [filename] → [reason]

        COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        You MUST commit before finishing. Uncommitted work gets a generic fallback message.

        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Process saved pages: &lt;summary&gt;

        Routed:
        - &lt;title&gt; → &lt;destination&gt;

        Triggered-By: cb procedure
        Phase: intake
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>

    <validate severity="review">
      <shell>
        saved=$(ls box/inbox/pages-saved/*.record.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        todo=$(ls box/inbox/pages-todo/*.record.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        remaining=$((saved + todo))
        questions=$(ls box/questions/intake-*.question.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        echo "Remaining in inbox: $remaining"
        echo "Questions created: $questions"
        # OK if items remain only if questions were created for them
        [ "$remaining" -eq 0 ] || [ "$questions" -gt 0 ]
      </shell>
      <instruction>
        Every page should either be routed to a destination, trashed,
        or have a question created asking the user what to do.
        Pages should not be left sitting in inbox without action.
      </instruction>
      <why>
        Unprocessed pages will sit in inbox forever. The agent must
        make a decision (or ask) for every item.
      </why>
    </validate>
  </step>
</procedure>
